.TH ACTIVE-INFINITY-CLI 1 "2026-10-31" "active-infinity-cli 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
active-infinity-cli \- encode, validate, hash and store Active Infinity modules
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B active-infinity-cli
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B active-infinity-cli
is the production command-line surface for the Active Infinity codec. Every
command calls the Rust reference, so bytes, hashes and redaction match the
library. Without
.B --output
commands that emit bytes write to standard output.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B encode \fIsource.active\fR [--name NAME] [--output PATH]
Compile Active text to canonical AINF. The module name does not affect the
content hash.
.TP
.B decode \fIimage.ainf\fR
Validate, then print the redacted JSON projection. Secret values never appear.
.TP
.B validate \fIimage.ainf\fR
Fail-closed validation; prints node and byte counts.
.TP
.B hash \fIimage.ainf\fR
Print the Blake3 content hash over the canonical image (64 hex characters).
.TP
.B stream \fIimage.ainf\fR
Reassemble an AINS stream and print the image hash.
.TP
.B store put \fIimage.ainf\fR [--root DIR]
.TQ
.B store get \fIhash\fR [--root DIR] [--output PATH]
Content-addressed local store (default root
.IR .active-store ).
.TP
.B dict train --output \fIdict\fR [--size N] \fIsample\fR...
Train a zstd dictionary. The default size is derived from the corpus; a size
larger than the samples can support is refused.
.TP
.B dict apply --dictionary \fIdict\fR [--decompress] [--level N] [--max-bytes N] \fIinput\fR
Compress with a dictionary, or decompress with an explicit output ceiling
(default 64 MiB).
.TP
.B bench \fIencode|decode|validate|hash\fR \fIfile\fR [--iterations N]
Local microbench; prints p50, p95 and p99 in nanoseconds.
.TP
.B conformance run [--manifest PATH]
Run the vector pack and print a JSON scorecard. Any failing case fails the
command.
.TP
.B doctor
Version, compiled features and exit codes.
.TP
.B help
Full usage with examples.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Validation, verification, I/O or codec failure. The message starts with the
stable
.I infinity/...
code.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error: unknown command, missing argument or bad flag.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
active-infinity-cli encode app.active --name app.active --output app.ainf
active-infinity-cli hash app.ainf
active-infinity-cli decode app.ainf
active-infinity-cli dict train --output frames.dict tests/vectors/valid/*.ainf
active-infinity-cli dict apply --dictionary frames.dict --output app.ainf.zst app.ainf
active-infinity-cli bench validate app.ainf --iterations 100
fi
.SH NOTES
Compression is transport and storage only: the content hash is always computed
over the uncompressed canonical image. Diagnostics never print secret payloads
or raw capability authority.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR active-rpc-cli (1)
